-- title:
--   Exactly q-1 minimal primes in the H₁ moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q\ell_g$-th root of unity $\xi$, and suppose some ring homomorphism $L \to \mathbb{C}$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ be the intersection of the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$ (the units $\equiv 1 \bmod q$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb{Z}/\ell_g)^\times$, and let $K \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ be the intermediate field generated over $L$ by the image, under coefficientwise extension along $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in its maximal ideal, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$, and let $j \in K$ have Laurent expansion the coefficient extension of the $q$-series of the $j$-function, with $j \ne 0$. Assume $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units in $A$. Further hypotheses, summarised here, are: equivariance of the level structures under variable change (preservation of $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points $D$ with $x_Q=x_P$, $y_Q=y_P$, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}(x_P)=0$; preservation of the cyclic-kernel conditions $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}$ under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and preservation of divisibility of `inLineMulPoly`), a family $\mathcal{G}$ of relative group laws on the projective models over $A$-algebras which is chord-tangent and has the origin as identity, a level transport $\mathcal{T}$ for Drinfeld pairs of level $q$ which is a section transport, and the existence of graded ring homomorphisms on projective-model graded rings realising variable changes and coefficient maps, dominating the irrelevant ideal. Let $P_0$ be a fine moduli package for the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A ℓg M' q …` — points are Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant, equipped with $\Gamma_0$-type cyclic kernel generators $h_p$ for $p \mid M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point, and a Drinfeld basis of the $q$-torsion, subject to the link condition $h_{\ell_g} \mid \mathrm{inLineMulPoly}(W,\ell_g,\ell_g^{v_{\ell_g}(M')-1},x_P)$, all taken up to variable change — with representing ring $P_0.B_0$ of finite type over $A$, and let $x$ be a point of this datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant, read in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$, is [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18). Then the set of minimal primes of the zero ideal of $P_0.B_0$ is finite and has exactly $q-1$ elements.
--
--   This counts the geometric components of the fine moduli ring for the level structure combining Drinfeld $q$-bases, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point and cyclic $\Gamma_0$-kernels at the primes of $M'$, in the presence of a Tate point whose $j$-invariant is the $q$-th power $q$-expansion: the components are indexed by the values of the Weil pairing $e_q$ of the Drinfeld basis, a set of size $\#(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times = q-1$. It feeds the downstream reduction, over constants generated by the Tate point data, to finiteness together with a bound of one minimal prime.
